WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:01.768 align:start size:94% position:6%
-How are you?
-I am great.

00:00:01.768 --> 00:00:02.635 line:92%
-I'm so happy to hear this.

00:00:02.635 --> 00:00:05.605 size:84% position:42%
I know that you go back
from recess tomorrow.

00:00:05.605 --> 00:00:06.072 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yes.

00:00:06.072 --> 00:00:07.874
-So tell me, during the recess,
do you miss it?

00:00:07.874 --> 00:00:09.242 line:92%
Do you miss your colleagues?

00:00:09.242 --> 00:00:13.313
Do you miss your colleagues from
the other side of the aisle?

00:00:13.313 --> 00:00:14.280 size:88% position:44% line:92%
-Let me put it this way.

00:00:14.280 --> 00:00:16.683 align:start size:94% position:6%
I am ready to get back
in the fight.

00:00:16.683 --> 00:00:17.884 align:start size:94% position:6%
-All right.
-Anytime.

00:00:17.884 --> 00:00:19.919 align:start size:94% position:6%
-There you go.
-That's my job.

00:00:19.919 --> 00:00:21.254 size:84% position:42% line:92%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:21.254 --> 00:00:21.921 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Wonderful to hear.

00:00:21.921 --> 00:00:26.192 align:start size:94% position:6%
I will say, your message
is a very strong one.

00:00:26.192 --> 00:00:29.662 align:start size:94% position:6%
I find it very counter
to what your favorite show is.

00:00:29.662 --> 00:00:32.832 align:start size:94% position:6%
When I think of what Elizabeth
Warren's favorite show is,

00:00:32.832 --> 00:00:36.736 align:start size:94% position:6%
I would not guess
that it is "Ballers."

00:00:36.736 --> 00:00:37.904 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:00:37.904 --> 00:00:39.506 align:start size:94% position:6%
-But it is.
-That's true. Okay.

00:00:39.506 --> 00:00:43.143
Because you did tweet, "To all
the reporters tweeting at me

00:00:43.143 --> 00:00:46.479 align:start size:94% position:6%
about the season premiere of
'Ballers' on Sunday night

00:00:46.479 --> 00:00:49.315 align:start size:94% position:6%
at 10:00 p.m.,
like I haven't had this date

00:00:49.315 --> 00:00:52.886
saved on my calendar for months:
I know."

00:00:52.886 --> 00:00:53.453 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-True. I know.

00:00:53.453 --> 00:00:55.655
-You know, and by the way,
someone else noticed your tweet.

00:00:55.655 --> 00:00:58.591
This is Dwayne "The Rock"
Johnson, the star of "Ballers."

00:00:58.591 --> 00:01:00.994 align:start size:94% position:6%
"You reporters
better put some respect

00:01:00.994 --> 00:01:01.694 line:92%
on Senator Warren's name.

00:01:01.694 --> 00:01:04.197 align:start size:94% position:6%
She is ready for our season
premiere of 'Ballers.'"

00:01:04.197 --> 00:01:06.633 align:start size:94% position:6%
And then, "Thank you, Senator,
for the support.

00:01:06.633 --> 00:01:08.068 align:start size:94% position:6%
I feel
we'll deliver our best yet.

00:01:08.068 --> 00:01:11.504 align:start size:94% position:6%
You have a big Rock-sized hug
coming when I see you."

00:01:11.504 --> 00:01:11.938 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Whoa.

00:01:11.938 --> 00:01:13.373 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I mean, that is --
-That's good.

00:01:13.373 --> 00:01:14.474 size:84% position:42% line:92%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:14.474 --> 00:01:15.442 line:92%
-I would say a Rock-size hug

00:01:15.442 --> 00:01:17.777 align:start size:94% position:6%
is both very exciting
and also very terrifying.

00:01:17.777 --> 00:01:20.113 size:88% position:44%
Just be a little careful
about a Rock-size hug.

00:01:20.113 --> 00:01:22.015 size:84% position:42%
-Yeah. It's a thing.
-You were here in 2014,

00:01:22.015 --> 00:01:25.652
and it seems very long ago you
were considered, at the time,

00:01:25.652 --> 00:01:28.154 align:start size:94% position:6%
the far left end of
the Democratic Party.

00:01:28.154 --> 00:01:31.558 align:start size:94% position:6%
There has been
a progressive wave, it seems,

00:01:31.558 --> 00:01:32.959 size:84% position:42% line:92%
post the 2016 election.

00:01:32.959 --> 00:01:35.395 align:start size:94% position:6%
Are you surprised
it took this long,

00:01:35.395 --> 00:01:39.032 align:start size:94% position:6%
or are you relieved
that it's finally happening?

00:01:39.032 --> 00:01:42.168 line:92%
-Oh, look, I look at this as

00:01:42.168 --> 00:01:45.905
people are starting to ask
the fundamental question.

00:01:45.905 --> 00:01:47.807 line:92%
Who does government work for?

00:01:47.807 --> 00:01:50.910 align:start size:94% position:6%
And, boy, has that become
even clearer

00:01:50.910 --> 00:01:52.612 line:92%
over the last year and a half.

00:01:52.612 --> 00:01:56.316 align:start size:94% position:6%
The Republicans passed
this gigantic tax giveaway.

00:01:56.316 --> 00:02:02.655
$1.5 trillion to giant
corporations and bazillionaires.

00:02:02.655 --> 00:02:05.425
That's who they think government
should work for,

00:02:05.425 --> 00:02:07.193 line:92%
that the rich and the powerful

00:02:07.193 --> 00:02:09.195 align:start size:94% position:6%
should get richer
and more powerful.

00:02:09.195 --> 00:02:13.032
My view on this and a lot of
folks around this country is,

00:02:13.032 --> 00:02:16.469 size:84% position:42%
no, government ought to
work for the people,

00:02:16.469 --> 00:02:18.972 align:start size:94% position:6%
and that's what
this fight is all about.

00:02:18.972 --> 00:02:19.672 size:81% position:41% line:92%
That's how I see this.

00:02:19.672 --> 00:02:23.910 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Was it frustrating for you
having been, you know,

00:02:23.910 --> 00:02:26.146
a politician who had always
talked about the middle class

00:02:26.146 --> 00:02:28.848
and actually taken steps
to protect the middle class

00:02:28.848 --> 00:02:31.084 align:start size:94% position:6%
to see Donald Trump
also frame himself

00:02:31.084 --> 00:02:32.218 line:92%
as a hero of the middle class?

00:02:32.218 --> 00:02:36.890 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Sure. But now, it's not
even about the words.

00:02:36.890 --> 00:02:39.792 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's about what have you
actually done?

00:02:39.792 --> 00:02:42.695 line:92%
You give away $1.5 trillion

00:02:42.695 --> 00:02:44.430
to the richest and most powerful
among us?

00:02:44.430 --> 00:02:46.566 align:start size:94% position:6%
I just want to think
for a minute

00:02:46.566 --> 00:02:47.767 size:88% position:44% line:92%
what you really could do

00:02:47.767 --> 00:02:50.770
if you were investing that money
in America.

00:02:50.770 --> 00:02:54.941 align:start size:94% position:6%
And on this,
I want to say for me,

00:02:54.941 --> 00:02:55.875 size:84% position:42% line:92%
this is really personal

00:02:55.875 --> 00:02:58.945 size:78% position:39%
because this is about
how government works.

00:02:58.945 --> 00:03:03.183 align:start size:94% position:6%
I grew up in one of these
paycheck-to-paycheck families.

00:03:03.183 --> 00:03:05.018 line:92%
My daddy ended up as a janitor.

00:03:05.018 --> 00:03:07.520
My mom worked a minimum-wage job
at Sears.

00:03:07.520 --> 00:03:14.327
My chance in life was a $50
a semester commuter college.

00:03:14.327 --> 00:03:15.962 line:92%
I grabbed it and hung on,

00:03:15.962 --> 00:03:18.598 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I got to be
a public schoolteacher.

00:03:18.598 --> 00:03:20.300 line:92%
I got to be a college professor,

00:03:20.300 --> 00:03:22.702 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I got to be
a United States Senator

00:03:22.702 --> 00:03:25.872 align:start size:94% position:6%
all because America
invested in kids like me.

00:03:25.872 --> 00:03:28.808 line:92%
I believe in that America.

00:03:28.808 --> 00:03:33.546 size:84% position:42% line:92%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:33.546 --> 00:03:36.082 size:84% position:42%
-Do you take -- I mean,
solace is a weird word,

00:03:36.082 --> 00:03:37.984 align:start size:94% position:6%
but have you --
do you find it notable

00:03:37.984 --> 00:03:40.486 align:start size:94% position:6%
that right now as we come
towards the midterms,

00:03:40.486 --> 00:03:42.121 align:start size:94% position:6%
it seems as though
the Republican Party

00:03:42.121 --> 00:03:46.125
is not actually running on this
tax bill they passed, which...

00:03:46.125 --> 00:03:46.659 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-No kidding.

00:03:46.659 --> 00:03:49.162
-...is the signature achievement
of the first half of

00:03:49.162 --> 00:03:50.430 line:92%
Donald Trump's term in office.

00:03:50.430 --> 00:03:53.900 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And stinks like
three-week-old garbage.

00:03:53.900 --> 00:03:54.767 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:03:54.767 --> 00:03:56.302 line:92%
I mean, they are, "Oh..."

00:03:56.302 --> 00:03:58.371 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know, somewhere else
every time

00:03:58.371 --> 00:04:00.440 align:start size:94% position:6%
anything about that tax bill
comes up.

00:04:00.440 --> 00:04:03.543 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know, and that's what's
remarkable about this.

00:04:03.543 --> 00:04:06.412 align:start size:94% position:6%
They passed it
knowing it was unpopular.

00:04:06.412 --> 00:04:08.648 size:75% position:38%
It's not like people
changed their minds.

00:04:08.648 --> 00:04:11.451 align:start size:94% position:6%
They passed it
knowing it was unpopular.

00:04:11.451 --> 00:04:15.321 align:start size:94% position:6%
Figured, "Hey, they'd spend
a few bazillion dollars

00:04:15.321 --> 00:04:16.155 size:78% position:39% line:92%
outrunning ads on it,

00:04:16.155 --> 00:04:19.459 align:start size:94% position:6%
and the American people
would fall for it."

00:04:19.459 --> 00:04:20.126 size:75% position:38% line:92%
And here's the deal.

00:04:20.126 --> 00:04:23.796
It's more unpopular now than it
was when it passed because,

00:04:23.796 --> 00:04:27.367
I think that really is the heart
of where America is.

00:04:27.367 --> 00:04:32.438
I think we still fundamentally,
fundamentally, down at our core,

00:04:32.438 --> 00:04:34.974 size:78% position:39%
believe in the things
we can do together.

00:04:34.974 --> 00:04:37.610 align:start size:94% position:6%
Believe in the things
like healthcare

00:04:37.610 --> 00:04:38.444 size:84% position:42% line:92%
is a basic human right,

00:04:38.444 --> 00:04:41.681 align:start size:94% position:6%
and our kids should be able
to get an education

00:04:41.681 --> 00:04:42.849 line:92%
without getting crushed by debt,

00:04:42.849 --> 00:04:46.552
and that seniors should be able
to retire with some dignity

00:04:46.552 --> 00:04:51.024 align:start size:94% position:6%
and that we're willing to pull
together to pitch in

00:04:51.024 --> 00:04:53.726 align:start size:94% position:6%
some of our money
to try to make that happen,

00:04:53.726 --> 00:04:58.831
to build a better future
for ourselves and for our kids.

